# Blog SEO Standards

Follow these rules when creating or editing blog posts to maximize organic visibility and growth.

## Frontmatter (Required)

Every post must have:

```yaml
---
title: "Keyword-rich, specific title (not generic)"
description: "Compelling meta description, 150-160 chars, includes primary keyword"
pubDate: YYYY-MM-DD
heroImage: "/images/blog/[slug]-hero.png"
author: "Brobot Media"
tags: ["Primary", "Secondary", "Brobot One", "Topic"]
---
```

- **title:** Include primary search phrase. Be specific (e.g. "How AI Phone Answering Cuts Missed Calls by 75%" not "Phone Tips").
- **description:** Sell the click. Include keyword + benefit. Used for search snippets and social previews.
- **heroImage:** Create a unique hero for each post. Path: `/images/blog/[slug]-hero.png`.
- **tags:** 3-5 tags. Include "Brobot One" when relevant. Use for related-post matching.

## Content Structure

- **Length:** 1,200–2,500 words. Competitive topics need depth.
- **H1:** Single H1 = page title (in frontmatter).
- **H2/H3:** Logical sections. Include keywords in headings where natural.
- **Intro:** First 100 words should state the value prop and include primary keyword.
- **Conclusion:** Key takeaways + clear CTA (links to `/ai-phone-crm` or `/contact`).

## Internal Linking

- **CTA block:** Every post ends with "Ready to build your own AI Agent?" linking to `/contact` and `/`.
- **Related posts:** Handled automatically by the template (shows 3 posts by shared tags).
- **In-body links:** When mentioning Brobot One, AI answering, CRM, etc., link to relevant pages (`/ai-phone-crm`, `/conversational-ai`, `/contact`) at least once.

## Keyword Targeting

- Target phrases people search for: "missed calls cost", "AI phone answering", "speed to lead", "Brobot One vs [competitor]", "voicemail alternatives", "small business AI", etc.
- Use stats and numbers (e.g. "75% reduction", "$126K per year") — they perform well in snippets.
- Include industry terms: HVAC, plumbing, dental, contractors, VoIP, CRM, lead capture.

## Technical (Handled by Template)

The blog template automatically provides:

- BlogPosting schema (author, datePublished, image, publisher)
- og:image = post hero (not default logo)
- Related posts section (internal links by tag)
- Canonical URLs, sitemap

## Style (See blog-content.mdc)

- No em dashes (—). Use commas, colons, or parentheses instead.
